# gofmt, golangci-lint and .githooks/pre-commit all assume LF. With
# core.autocrlf=true -- the usual Windows default, and what this repo is
# developed under -- a plain `git checkout` hands the file back as CRLF,
# and gofmt then rejects the whole file on its line endings alone. That
# reads as "your code is unformatted" when nothing is wrong with it, and
# it fires on whichever file someone happened to check out last.
#
# The hook itself is the sharper edge: it is a POSIX shell script, and a
# CRLF copy breaks the shebang outright on Linux.
#
# Pin the working tree here so none of this depends on how any one clone
# has autocrlf set. Blobs are already stored LF, so this changes nothing
# in history -- only what lands on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Embedded verbatim by internal/infra/render; keep every text filter off.
*.otf binary
